# DataSource Pattern

```kotlin
interface {Feature}RemoteDataSource : RemoteDataSource {
    suspend fun get{Items}(token: String): ApiResponse<List<{Feature}Dto>>
    suspend fun get{Item}ById(token: String, id: String): ApiResponse<{Feature}Dto>
    suspend fun create{Item}(token: String, request: Create{Feature}Request): ApiResponse<{Feature}Dto>
}

@Inject
class {Feature}RemoteDataSourceImpl(
    private val httpClient: HttpClient,
    private val logger: FleetLogger
) : {Feature}RemoteDataSource {

    private val baseUrl = "${ApiConfig.BASE_URL}/{features}"

    override suspend fun get{Items}(token: String): ApiResponse<List<{Feature}Dto>> {
        return httpClient.get(baseUrl) {
            headers { append(HttpHeaders.Authorization, "Bearer $token") }
        }.body()
    }
}
```

## Rules
- Interface + Impl split. Interface in `data/datasource/`, impl in same file or separate
- Base URL from `ApiConfig.BASE_URL` + resource path
- Auth via `Bearer $token` header on every request
- Return `ApiResponse<T>` (or typed response wrapper), not raw `HttpResponse`
- Log requests/responses with `FleetLogger`, tag with module constant
- Query params via `url { parameters.append("key", "value") }`
